From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sean Dolbec <sdolbec1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:51:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: apple: pmp-report: Use the retained T8132
 predicate

Use the shared retained T8132 predicate for the report readiness path.
The prior test already selected the T8132 report for a compatible T8132
supplier on the qualified firmware path. The new predicate additionally
requires the machine compatible apple,t8132; it does not newly enable
J773g. Update the host fixtures to provide the same helper.

A prior J773g bring-up stack sent and received an AGX request with its
PMP report present. This refactoring has not been isolated on hardware.

Signed-off-by: Sean Dolbec <sdolbec1@gmail.com>
[dylan: one tool trailer of the original message is not reproduced here]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c    | 3 ++-
 tools/asahi/t6030-pmp-graph-tests.c    | 7 +++++++
 tools/asahi/t6030-pmp-supplier-tests.c | 7 +++++++
 3 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
index 7ce01a88bb..b40fb8bbcc 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/apple/pmp-report.c
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@
 #include <linux/seq_file.h>
 #include <linux/sizes.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
+#include <linux/soc/apple/pmp-display.h>
 #include <linux/soc/apple/pmp-report.h>
 #include <linux/soc/apple/t8132.h>
 #include <linux/string.h>
@@ -623,7 +624,7 @@ int apple_pmp_report_wait_supplier_ready(struct device *supplier, unsigned int t
 	struct platform_device *pdev;
 	struct apple_pmp_report *rep;
 	u64 status;
-	bool t8132 = apple_t8132_firmware_path() &&
+	bool t8132 = apple_pmp_t8132_retained_board() &&
 		of_device_is_compatible(supplier->of_node, "apple,t8132-pmp-v2");
 	int ret;
 
diff --git a/tools/asahi/t6030-pmp-graph-tests.c b/tools/asahi/t6030-pmp-graph-tests.c
index e89d982d2d..1a18e24165 100644
--- a/tools/asahi/t6030-pmp-graph-tests.c
+++ b/tools/asahi/t6030-pmp-graph-tests.c
@@ -478,6 +478,13 @@ static inline bool apple_t8132_firmware_path(void)
 {
 	return apple_t8132_air();
 }
+
+/* Production: <linux/soc/apple/pmp-display.h>. */
+static inline bool apple_pmp_t8132_retained_board(void)
+{
+	return apple_t8132_firmware_path() &&
+	       of_machine_is_compatible("apple,t8132");
+}
 static bool of_property_read_bool(const struct device_node *n, const char *p)
 {
 	if (!strcmp(p, "apple,always-on"))
diff --git a/tools/asahi/t6030-pmp-supplier-tests.c b/tools/asahi/t6030-pmp-supplier-tests.c
index 59c2c0d3cd..4dbadfee51 100644
--- a/tools/asahi/t6030-pmp-supplier-tests.c
+++ b/tools/asahi/t6030-pmp-supplier-tests.c
@@ -172,6 +172,13 @@ static inline bool apple_t8132_firmware_path(void)
 {
 	return apple_t8132_air();
 }
+
+/* Production: <linux/soc/apple/pmp-display.h>. */
+static inline bool apple_pmp_t8132_retained_board(void)
+{
+	return apple_t8132_firmware_path() &&
+	       of_machine_is_compatible("apple,t8132");
+}
 static struct device_node *of_find_compatible_node(struct device_node *from,
 						   const char *type,
 						   const char *compat)
-- 
2.43.0

